<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiang Yu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xiang Yu was a Chinese military leader who led the rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> and became the dominant warlord after its fall. He then fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> for control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the Chu–Han contention. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> describe how Liu Bang, a minor official of peasant origin, outmanoeuvred his aristocratic rival Xiang Yu and established the Han Dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xiang-yu.jpg" alt="Xiang Yu" width="289" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Chinese artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portraits_of_Famous_Men_-_Xiang_Wang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
